course: dictionary
lesson: 10727
title: Upgrade: better, newer, higher
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Upgrade can be a verb (to upgrade) or a noun (an upgrade). When you upgrade something, you make it better, newer or more powerful, like a phone or a computer. An upgrade is the better version itself, or the change that makes it better.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Nobody invented fire, farming began in several lands on its own, and the Stone, Bronze and Iron Ages are labels historians made, not days when everyone upgraded together like in a game.» Here upgraded means got better or moved on to a new stage, like levelling up in a game. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? Try "improved" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Upgrade can also mean raising a level. A weather report might upgrade a storm to a hurricane, which means the storm is now stronger and more dangerous. Hotels and planes can upgrade you to a better room or seat. The clue is the word around it: the storm, the room, or the seat.
explain: Upgrade is not always good. «Upgrading words is good until it isn't: "He ambulated to the edifice" for "He walked to the building" sounds like a robot swallowed a dictionary.» The writer is saying that a fancier word is not always a better word. The goal is the right word, not the longest one.
fact: Upgrade can be a verb or a noun.
fact: To upgrade something means to make it better, newer or more powerful.
fact: An upgrade is a better or newer version, or the change that makes it better.
fact: To upgrade a storm or warning means to raise its level.
fact: Phrases you may hear include «upgrade to», «a free upgrade» and «software upgrade».
exercise: «He wanted to upgrade his old phone, so he bought a newer one.» What does upgrade mean here? | To paint something a new colour | To throw something away for ever | To lose something on purpose | *To make something better or newer
exercise: «The weather office upgraded the storm to a hurricane.» What does upgraded mean? | Gave it a name for children | *Raised its level, making it more dangerous | Stopped it from moving | Made it smaller and weaker
exercise: Dad says, «We got a free upgrade to a bigger room at the hotel.» What is a free upgrade? | Checking out early | *Being moved to a better room at no cost | Paying double for a smaller room | Staying in the same room
test: In a game, Ella says, «I will upgrade my sword before the next level.» What does upgrade mean? | To sell the sword | To break the sword | *To make the sword better and stronger | To hide the sword
test: Why is «He ambulated to the edifice» a weak example of upgrading words? | Walking is always a bad thing to write about | Edifice means a happy dog | *It uses a long, fancy word where a simple one, «walked to the building», works better | It is too short to be understood
exam: «The school will upgrade its computers next year.» Which word means nearly the same as upgrade? | *Improve | Forget | Sell | Hide
